        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(B) False</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text">The event loop interleaves coroutines, switching between them at <code>await</code> points. Only one coroutine executes at any given instant. This is concurrency (interleaving), not parallelism (simultaneous execution). Think: one chef, many dishes — never two burners at the exact same moment.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Q4 -->
  <div class="quiz-card">
    <div class="quiz-card-header">
      <span class="quiz-q-num">Q 04</span>
      <span class="quiz-type-tag">Multiple Choice</span>
    </div>
    <p class="quiz-question">What kind of work does <code>async</code>/<code>await</code> help with?</p>
