    <div class="quiz-answer">
      <div class="quiz-answer-inner">
        <div class="quiz-answer-highlight">✓ Correct: <strong>(B) I/O-bound work</strong></div>
        <p class="quiz-answer-text">Async shines when your code spends time <em>waiting</em> for external responses. During that wait, the event loop handles other requests. CPU-bound work doesn't have wait points, so async provides no benefit — you need multiple workers (processes) for that.</p>
